With the top cover off the 5305 won't power up at all. Doug wrote that the
system does power up and, after a variable period of time, suddenly powers
off again.
What makes me wonder is that variable period of time, especially the
duration
that Doug specifies: it may take a couple of minutes or just a few seconds.

A couple of questions:

1) how far does the 5305 get in the start up process ?
     like does it pass POST?
     is the OS still able to boot?
2) is there any pattern in the length of the "power on" period?
     i.e. the first power up period is several minutes and they get shorter
after each try?
     (I realize that this is a leading question :-)
3) did you add any new hardware recently
      - new disk
      - second cpu
      - more memory
      - or just open the box and rearranged some flat cables?
4) experiment:
     Run the 5305 on one power supply only. The manual states that it needs
two
     to operate but I discovered that a single cpu machine with 512 MB and 8
disks
    will run on one power supply.

The way Doug describes the problem it is most likely a heat problem. Second
guess
is a capacitor slowly going south in the power supplies.

Hans

PS
On PDP-11's and VAXes one could run hardware diagnostics. Is there anything
similar for the AlphaServer 1200 / Digital Server 5305?




