Congratulations with the 5305! You might need to check a couple of things if
you
want to run Tru64 on it:
- what kind of SCSI controller does it have?
- memory configuration: I tried Tru64 5.0 on a 5305 and that did not
install. Tru64 complained about a memory
  hole and the installation panic-ed. My 5305 has 2 x 128MB as well as 8 x
32MB. (memory goes in pairs)
  The memory slot position determines the base address of the memory module
installed. So in case of the 32MB
  cards there's a 96 MB "hole" in the address space. VMS has no problems
with that, Tru64 V5.0 does.
  I tried Debian and RedHat on the 5305 as well and they did not install
either. Error messages ranged from the
  very informative ** oops ** to just "panic". Tru64 V5.0 runs fine on a
Digital Server 3300.
- you must modify the nvram file, see http://home.zonnet.nl/hvlems for
instructions
The witebox alpha's are NT only, but with very little effort they will run
VMS (and cheaper than Tru64)...

Hans




