that amount) then it might
explain my problems with Linux and Tru64. BTW I used SRM for the
installation attempts.
AlphaBIOS is the default console interface but it is easily changed to SRM.
I had to replace the "NT only Sym53C875" controller with a KZPCM SYM53C875
SCSI controller
to make it work with VMS.
The 5305 and the 1200 are very similar, to the extent that the 5305 can use
a 1200-cpu and memory.
But there's no support and that reduces the price for the white box alpha's,
to zero even, and that makes
them excellent hobby systems.
I can put up an ISO file of the Tru64 cd's if you like?

Hans




