Dear Jazzy & list:

This book is pretty good

Tru64 Unix System Administrator's Guide
by Matthew Cheek (Author), Scott Fafrak (Author), Steven Hancock
(Author), Martin Moore (Author), Gregory Yates (Author)

as well as O'Reilly's 

Essential System Administration, 3rd Edition 
By �leen Frisch
3rd Edition August 2002 
ISBN: 0-596-00343-9

A good starter system IMHO is the PWS 500 a or au (Miata), with a
KZPSAxx raid controller. Hook that to a BA 356 array - get the blue
one, and find a set of the 9.1G disks in blue hot-swap sleds.

Miata class machines have a PCI bus and use readily available SDRAM. 
The DEC version of the Mylex DAC 960 is the controller card to get-
U2wide, no major problems. You can use the Mylex unit but you have to
flash it with DEC firmware before the system firmware (SRM) will see
it.

You can pick up a Miata on EBay for a little over $100 and the KZPSA
cards seem to go for around $25.  The best bet for the array is to
find one with all its disks - you might have to pay over $100.  Make
sure you get the personality module.

This site has a lot of info on setting up your array.  Read it first
so you'll know hat to look for on eBay.

http://h30097.www3.hp.com/docs/cluster_doc/cluster_15/TCR_HWCFG/CHNTRXXX.HTM

An alternative would be an AlphaServer or Ultimate Workstation, both
of which have a row or stack of hot-swap disks built into the case. 
Of the two options I would go with the Ultimate workstation.  Don't
pay over $300 and amke sure it is full of disks.

good luck

jn


