If you have another VMS system on your network, there are some potential
tricks that you can play.  Backup the CD-ROM to a disk image, transfer it
via the network to the VAXstation 4, and restore it to one of the HD's. 
Then boot off that hard drive and install on the other one.  I used this
trick to install 7.2 on a MicroVAX III using RA72 and RA73 disks.

