Lets be clear here about what you have.

You have VT510 terminals which speak ASCII over RS232.
You say you have a DECserver which means you don't need to have Digiboards.
The two are exclusive of each other. Could you be mistaken.

If you are mistaken about the Digiboards, and you really do have the
terminals all plugged into a DECserver then in fact the DECserver is
speaking Telnet to the UNIX server, unless it is a Tru64 UNIX server, then
it could all be speaking LAT.

If you are mistaken that you have a DECserver and you really do have
Digiboards, then you have to extend the Digiboard interfaces to the patch
panel that the terminals are plugged into.

