> by far the easiest method is by using simh.
> Download simh from http://simh.trailing-edge.com/ and install it on a PC
> with your preferred OS.
> Make an ISO image from the VAX/VMS distribution CD.
> The simh boot file must point to a new file on disk which will serve as
its
> own system disk;
> the associated device must be RA82 or RA90. The other disk must be defined
> as a CDROM
> and attech it to the ISO file.
> Boot from the ISO file and install VMS and DECnet on the simulator.
>
> At this point you have two options:
> - create a second data disk on simh and create an image backup of the
CDROM
> drive.
>   Copy the BACKUP saveset to the VAX with DECnet (or IP if you like)
>   BACK/IMAGE the SAVEset to a spare disk on the "real" VAX and boot from
it.
>   Repeat the install procedure on the real hardware
> - use cluster_config.com to set up a network cluster; allow the satellite
as
> a disk server.
>   Boot the real VAX from the newly created root on the SIMH VAX
>   Once the node is up, backup/image the  CDROM drive to a local disk on
the
> real VAX.
>   Boot from that disk and install VMS
>
> Hans
>
