Richard Tomkins <tomkinsr@istop.com> wrote:
>  The RQDX4 was used for RX35, RD50/1/2/3/4 drives.

> The RD51 was a Seagate ST-412, the 2 a Quantum 540, the 3 a Micropolis 1325
> or 1335 and the 4 was a Maxtor XT-2190D

Not quite that simple... there were two different drives (from different
manufacturers) called RD51, and four different RD52 (though I think only
two got into the wild).  You can find some of the information about the
variants in the XXDP listings.  There's also an RD31 and RD32, both
Seagate (20MB and 40MB, though I can't remember the exact model numbers
offhand).

I've never seen an RQDX4 either.  Was it some special MicroVAX-specific
board?  It's not one of the normal QBus ones, those are RQDX1 and RQDX2
(the quad-height ones) and RQDX3 (dual-height, in various different
firmware versions).

