This weekend I was able to successfully flash the BIOS to V1.12 and
gain full support for my 10GB drive! I think the problem was that
jumper #1 was in the on position when I first tried to flash. This was
the position it was in when I first opened the system case and it
doesn't say in the flash instructions that this would prevent the
process from completing, but when I tried flashing with this jumper
config:

1 - off
2 - off
3 - off
4 - off
5 - on (switch in down position - to enable flash update)
6 - off
7 - off
8 - on

...it worked!

Ben, thanks for your help. I might have given up if you hadn't told me
to check the jumpers again. I think I'm going to live with the 200 mhz
speed, the bigger, newer drive has made things a little faster
anyways.

Thanks again for your insight.

-Bob

